---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import media from "../data/media.json";

// The photographs whose captions are camera filenames, or which hedge. The
// tree attaches a name to most of them; a filename is not evidence that the
// name is right, and this page exists to be shown to somebody who would know.
const CAM = /^(img[_-]?\s*\d+|dsc\w*\d+|scan\s*\d+|\d{6,}(\.\d+)?([+.]\S*)?|photo\s*\d*|image\d*)$/i;
const HEDGE = /\bmaybe\b|\bunnamed\b|\?|granny heddies photos-\d+/i;
const strip = (c) => (c || "").replace(/\.(jpe?g|png|tiff?)$/i, "").trim();

const photos = media.filter((m) => m.kind === "photograph");
const rank = (m) => {
  const c = strip(m.caption);
  if (!c || CAM.test(c)) return "filename";
  if (HEDGE.test(c)) return "hedged";
  return "named";
};
const ask = photos.filter((m) => rank(m) !== "named");
const filename = ask.filter((m) => rank(m) === "filename");
const hedged = ask.filter((m) => rank(m) === "hedged");
const named = photos.filter((m) => rank(m) === "named");
---
<Base title="The Faces"
  eyebrow={`${ask.length} photographs this archive cannot vouch for`}
  dek="A contact sheet meant to be shown to somebody in the family. Every picture here is attached to a name in the tree — but the caption underneath it is a camera filename or a hedge, so the name is somebody's recollection rather than a record. One afternoon with a relative would close most of this page.">

  <section class="blk">
    <p class="lede">This is the one open question in the archive that <strong>no archive can
    answer</strong>. A parish register will eventually give up a birth date; nothing in Rijeka or
    Gospić will ever say which of two women in a photograph is Milka. The people who could say are
    alive, and the pictures have never been put in front of them in one place. That is all this
    page is.</p>

    <div class="qa">
      <h3>What is being asked, exactly</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li><strong>Is the person named actually the person shown?</strong> The name comes from
          where the file sits in the tree, not from anything written on the picture.</li>
        <li><strong>Who else is in it?</strong> Several are groups, and only one person is
          tagged.</li>
        <li><strong>Roughly when, and where?</strong> A decade and a town would let each one be
          checked against the ages of the people in it.</li>
        <li><strong>Is anything written on the back?</strong> Studio stamps date and place a
          photograph better than anything else here.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">{filename.length} with no caption at all</div>
    <h2>The camera kept the only name these have</h2>
    <p class="lede">Uploaded straight off a phone or a scanner. <span class="mono">scan0051</span>,
    <span class="mono">1134835622</span> — the number is a timestamp, and it dates the
    <em>scanning</em>, not the photograph.</p>
    <div class="photos">
      {filename.map((m) => (
        <figure class="doc">
          <a href={u("/photos/line/" + m.file)}>
            <img src={u("/photos/line/" + m.file)} alt={m.caption} loading="lazy" /></a>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="mono dim">{strip(m.caption)}</span>
            <br />{m.people.length > 0
              ? <span>Tree says: {m.people.map((p, i) => (
                  <span>{i > 0 && ", "}{p.slug
                    ? <a href={u("/people/" + p.slug)}>{p.name}</a> : p.name}</span>))}</span>
              : <span class="warn">Nobody tagged at all</span>}
          </figcaption>
        </figure>))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">{hedged.length} where the caption itself hedges</div>
    <h2>Somebody was already unsure</h2>
    <p class="lede">These carry a name and a doubt in the same breath — <em>“maybe Peco”</em>,
    <em>“unnamed”</em>. Whoever wrote the caption is the best witness this archive has, and they
    were not certain either.</p>
    <div class="photos">
      {hedged.map((m) => (
        <figure class="doc">
          <a href={u("/photos/line/" + m.file)}>
            <img src={u("/photos/line/" + m.file)} alt={m.caption} loading="lazy" /></a>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>{strip(m.caption)}</strong>
            <br />{m.people.map((p, i) => (
              <span>{i > 0 && ", "}{p.slug
                ? <a href={u("/people/" + p.slug)}>{p.name}</a> : p.name}</span>))}
          </figcaption>
        </figure>))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">Excluded from the count</div>
    <h2>Five “photographs” that are not photographs</h2>
    <p class="lede">Five items in the media library were being published as portraits of ancestors.
    They are <strong>stock question-mark graphics</strong> — placeholders uploaded to the tree for
    people who have no picture — and one still carries a visible
    <strong>Adobe Stock watermark</strong>.</p>
    <table class="reg">
      <thead><tr><th>Filed under</th><th>Born</th><th>What it actually is</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Michael Žubrinić</td><td class="mono">1811</td>
          <td>Red question-mark icon, watermarked</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Maria Catharina Orešković</td><td class="mono">1835</td>
          <td>The same icon, same watermark</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Josephum Antić</td><td class="mono">1806</td><td>Red question mark on white</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Maria Jelličić</td><td class="mono">1809</td><td>The same graphic</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Georgius “Jure” Antić Papić</td><td class="mono">1838</td><td>The same graphic</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="margin-top:1.2rem">The dates are the giveaway: a photograph of a man born in
    <strong>1806</strong> would be remarkable, and four of these five people died before or barely
    into the age of portrait photography. The build now drops anything marked
    <span class="mono">excluded</span> in
    <span class="mono">sources/media/classification.json</span>, so a placeholder cannot be shown as
    an ancestor's face. <a href={u("/corrections/")}>What changed →</a></p>
    <p class="dek">A sixth item was reclassified rather than dropped: a picture captioned
    <em>“Ljubomir Blazevic”</em> is a photograph of the <a href={u("/grave/")}>family gravestone</a>,
    not a portrait of him. It is a document and now sits with the documents.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">For contrast</div>
    <h2>The {named.length} that do carry a real caption</h2>
    <p class="lede">Not certain either — a caption is still somebody's memory — but at least
    somebody wrote a name rather than letting a file manager do it.</p>
    <ul class="cols">{named.map((m) => (
      <li><span class="mono">{strip(m.caption)}</span></li>))}</ul>
    <p style="margin-top:1.2rem"><a class="btn" href={u("/pictures/")}>All the pictures →</a>
      {" "}<a class="btn" href={u("/open-questions/")}>The open questions →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
